From: Jonathan Schwender <jschwender@posteo.net>
Date: Mon, 31 Aug 2026 11:01:27 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] docs: document how to update local branches after a sync

The runbook gains an "After a sync: updating your branches" section: the
routine pull --rebase path (fork-point + patch-id), the cases where it
trips, and the deterministic
`git rebase --onto sync/<date> pre-sync/<date> <branch>` form the tags
guarantee. CONTRIBUTING.md points at it.

Lands as an ordinary commit between syncs; the next sync's fold step
merges it into the runbook patch.

Validation: not required (documentation-only); uv run docs/ohos-sync/check_stack.py base/2026-08-29 passes.
AI-assisted: Yes (agent session; drafted from the maintainer's review question)
Signed-off-by: Jonathan Schwender <jschwender@posteo.net>
